                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I had a good time with this game.\nThere is something satisfying about killing tons of the enemies with the bloop death sound effect, and the way they dissapear. The mechanic of having to upgrade the enemies after each wave was an interesting idea and worked well for the gameplay.\n\n--BUGS--\nThere weren't very many bugs on release day. (The time I'm writing this review.)\n- The only gamebreaking one was when the enemies stopped spawning. It only happened once, but was still very annoying when it happened.\n- [strike] The unlocking the lava level 1 achievement didn't unlock. [/strike]\n- [strike]One enemy spawned inside the floor. [/strike]\n\nOther than that bug, the game is pretty well balanced and polished.\n\n--Unlockables--\nThere are plenty of unlockable outfits for the player and enemies to keep you going for the duration of the game.\nLots of achievements as well. (Although the playing 1,000 rounds seems a little too much for me.)\nIt definately added to my enjoyment of the game.\n\nLast but not least... The Pricing!\nI beat the game in 3.4 hours.\n$7 is a little much for 3.4 hours in my opinion, and would be a deterrent for me had I not recieved it for free.\nEspecially since when I completed the game, I felt like there should be more. (Especially another variant or two of the boss that comes every 5 rounds.)\n$5 seems more reasonable.\nOr maybe I'm just being a cheap fuck.\nBut if your willing to spend the cash, I think it would be worth your time.\nAlthough I beat it, I can still see myself coming back in the future for another round or two so I'll probably end up spending more than 3.4 hours on it. Oh well.",
